<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Real Africa Holdings headline EPS up 40 pct.</title>
<headline>Real Africa Holdings headline EPS up 40 pct.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		25.2	  vs 18.0</p>
<p>    - attrib		  31.0	  vs 20.7</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  -	    vs  -</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   71.04	 vs 40.89</p>
<p>Equity accounted earnings</p>
<p>    - dividends	     15.38	 vs 14.78</p>
<p>- share of retained</p>
<p>	earnings		50.87	 vs 28.12</p>
<p>    Interest income	 17.29	 vs 4.84</p>
<p>    Operating costs	  6.44	 vs 5.64</p>
<p>    Tax			  6.04	 vs 3.13</p>
<p>Full name: Real African Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said satisfactory growth was expected in the forthcoming year but no dividend was declared since it was considered prudent to preserve cash for prospective investments.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
